                            <comment id="15853010" author="zjffdu" created="Sun, 5 Feb 2017 00:49:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;livy test could be merged into spark 1.6 when livy 0.3 is released in the near future.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;BTW, Usually my own travis CI would finish quicker when apache travis CI is busy. Is it possible to only run my own travis CI without triggering apache travis CI ? so that we won&apos;t block in the apache travis CI queue. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15855588" author="jongyoul" created="Tue, 7 Feb 2017 08:55:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Personally, I agree with removing Spark 1.4 and 1.5. How about emailing this issue?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15855748" author="moon" created="Tue, 7 Feb 2017 10:51:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Another thing can save some build time is,&lt;br/&gt;
Currently we have 4 test profiles that builds all modules and test all modules.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;# Test all modules with spark 2.1.0 and scala 2.11&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;# Test all modules with spark 2.0.2 and scala 2.11&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;# Test all modules with scala 2.10&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;# Test all modules with scala 2.11&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;I think we can keep only 2 test profile to build/test all modules for scala 2.10 and scala 2.11, &lt;br/&gt;
and other 2 test profile is okay build and test only spark interpreter.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
